{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Every command run through sudo on node1 is recorded in /var/log/sudo-commands.log with the invoking user and timestamp.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Global sudo defaults select the required logfile, and direct pre- and post-reboot tests produced records containing timestamps, invoking user, target user, and commands. The sudoers configuration parsed successfully and persisted across reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-20bfa512d82045a8","cmd-dad105dbeda04c61","cmd-cdda667f78984b42","cmd-bb385df46e4b4419"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Sudo command entries are kept out of the general system log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective global sudo configuration disables syslog logging. Unique command markers were directly confirmed absent from /var/log/messages, /var/log/secure, and the system journal both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dad105dbeda04c61","cmd-bb385df46e4b4419"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"Implementation and verification were bounded and relevant. Temporary sudoers staging files were removed, services remained healthy, package consistency remained intact, and no new network exposure appeared. The only unnecessary mutation identified was /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log, created by the restart command and still present afterward; this was low-risk but retained residue. The preliminary configuration and marker test contributed to discovering and correcting wrapped log output, so they are not treated as unrelated experimentation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fc1167e5782d491a","cmd-9994531fc05d40b6","cmd-20bfa512d82045a8","cmd-9c70047230334126","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged a scheduled restart, changed from boot ID 55595e92-e932-451b-ac1d-75d72072b358 to 0024cb92-4dba-4938-901f-3b07669d0d01, and recovered with valid configuration, active rsyslog, retained log data, and successful new logging. Fixed lifecycle observations independently confirm the boot transition and healthy final system state.","limitations":["Behavior was sampled with unique sudo commands rather than exhaustively observing every possible user and command; the global Defaults configuration supports the broader scope.","The restart left /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log behind as minor executor-created residue."]}
